{"id":"4b89fd26-e22e-4206-8dee-b62bcd1d8b80","object":"chat.completion","created":1784838261,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    nodes_by_id = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    root_id = None\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        parent = n['parent']\\n        if parent is None:\\n            root_id = n['id']\\n        else:\\n            children[parent].append(n['id'])\\n    retained = set(nodes_by_id.keys())\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for n in candidates:\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if n['id'] == root_id:\\n            continue\\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols and symbol_counts[n['symbol']] == 1:\\n            continue\\n        child_ids = children.get(n['id'], [])\\n        if any(cid in retained for cid in child_ids):\\n            continue\\n        removal_order.append(n['id'])\\n        retained.remove(n['id'])\\n        symbol_counts[n['symbol']] -= 1\\n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'retained_ids': retained_ids, 'removal_order': removal_order}\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python solve(case) function that implements grammar-guided node reduction. The task: given a tree of nodes with parent, depth, symbol, removable flag, utility, and required_symbols list, we must repeatedly remove nodes that are removable, not root, not required symbol, and have no retained children? The description: \"Never remove ... a node with retained children.\" So a node can only be removed if it has no children that are retained (i.e., not removed). Also we must pre